  "details": "During the Town Hall on 7/20, with many users present, the uSpeak audio appeared to start dropping all packets. My guess is that the audio server died. This issue occurred even when most/all users were quiet. The two or three times it occurred, it seemed to happen around 48-50 users. The log is filled with lines like this:\n\n[Log:7/20/2017 9:08:40 PM] <color=white>uSpeak (31): QueuePacket (discarding old packet 2357 at index 309, estimated 41.28s late</color>\n\nMany logs were uploaded on Slack in the #bugreports channel.",
